# policy_target run matrix (read by scripts/launch.sh) -- FINAL (multi-seed).
#
# Working length SIM=20M, victim ALU=40 (widened the single-PC near-binary knee).
# Multi-victim sweep: 3 seeds (v_s0/1/2) x each neighbor x each config, so every duty
# gets a cross-seed mean +/- spread (the make-or-break for setpoint control on a steep
# slope). Light calibration points (cached on-traces) fit the curve / monotone / degree;
# the three ver_f* duties are the setpoint targets, their on_lines from the ALU=40 @20M
# inversion (f0*=0.25->on19, 0.50->on21, 0.75->on35).
#
# Output .out: <victim>_<neighbor>_<config>.out (consumed by rollup.py).

victim   v_s0  victim.c  0
victim   v_s1  victim.c  1
victim   v_s2  victim.c  2

# calibration (curve/monotone/degree) -- cached on-traces
neighbor cal_on08  attacker.c   8  72
neighbor cal_on16  attacker.c  16  64
neighbor cal_on20  attacker.c  20  60
neighbor cal_on24  attacker.c  24  56
neighbor cal_on32  attacker.c  32  48
neighbor cal_on48  attacker.c  48  32

# verification setpoints (new on-traces)
neighbor ver_f25  attacker.c  19  61
neighbor ver_f50  attacker.c  21  59
neighbor ver_f75  attacker.c  35  45

config   aware   aware.ini
config   blind   blind.ini
